  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A source of constant voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> is connected to a resistance<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> and two ideal inductors <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> through a switch <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> as shown. There is no mutual inductance between the two inductors. The switch <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> is initially open. At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> , the switch is closed and current begins to flow. Which of the following options is/are correct?<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/446324a5-f822-43ab-913b-f02aeb4331ea-image.png\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wt3al",
      "text": "The ratio of the currents through <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is fixed at all times <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "AXUZE",
      "text": "After a long time, the current through <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> will be <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Euru5",
      "text": "After a long time, the current through <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> will be <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "iRdnx",
      "text": "At  <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> , the current through the resistance R is  <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/88462d42-ccf9-4995-ab83-a4096c0bb7e7-image.png\"/> </p><p>As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are in parallel so equivalent  </p><p>inductance, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Here, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are the inductance (shown in circuit)</p><p>The current through the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>RL</mi></math> series circuit at anytime is given as </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>Rt</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>After a longtime i.e. at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>∞</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mo>∞</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Let currents through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> respectively. As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are joined in parallel</p><p>Voltage across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo></math> Voltage across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfrac><mrow><mo>d</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfrac><mrow><mo>d</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>Thus, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>By current division rule,</p><p>Current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p>Current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math></p>",
